# qmesh_npu — what is and isn't versioned
#
# Versioned: the build/verify/bench scripts, their logs, and the runnable
# `hvx/` package (llama.cpp b10288 built with the native Hexagon HVX backend).
# Everything below is either re-downloadable, re-buildable, third-party, or
# secret.

# --- Qualcomm Hexagon SDK (3.3 GB extracted + 818 MB tarball) -----------------
# Re-download: https://github.com/snapdragon-toolchain/hexagon-sdk/releases
#              /download/v6.6.0.0/hexagon-sdk-v6.6.0.0-arm64-wos.tar.xz
hexagon-sdk-wos/
*.tar.xz

# --- llama.cpp source clone (has its own .git; would become a broken gitlink) -
# Re-clone at tag b10288 (commit 360e134) and apply CMakeUserPresets.json.
llama.cpp/

# --- build + install outputs (regenerate with build_hvx.ps1 / stage_hvx.ps1) --
pkg-hvx/
pkg-snapdragon/
pkg-signed/
build-*/

# --- third-party prebuilt binaries, re-downloadable ---------------------------
b10150/
adreno/
tools/
*.zip

# --- SECRET: HTP code-signing private key. Never commit. ----------------------
# The public cert (ggml-htp-v1.cer) IS committed so the signed libggml-htp.cat
# can be verified; the .pfx that signs it must stay local.
certs/*.pfx
certs/*.pvk

# --- runtime scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
npu_server.pid
npu_server.out
npu_server.err
v.out
v.err
rpc_out.txt
rpc_err.txt
ab/
